# Fixed 2026-10-03, defect 170, lane depth.
# Symptom: 3,000 variants nested by value, `variant R<i>` holding `R<i-1>`,
# checked at exit 0 and stopped `build` at exit 2, *internal error: compiling
# the generated C failed* over clang's crash report, *Illegal instruction: 4*
# (Apple clang 21 on arm64 macOS; the CI's Apple clang died at 1,000). The
# crash also wrote 8,270,409 bytes of preprocessed C and a script into the
# system's temporary folder.
# Cause: clang converts a struct to its own form the first time a function
# needs it and recurses into every struct it holds by value, so a chain met
# from its top took a recursion as deep as the chain, 9,000 structs here,
# past clang's own 8 MB stack (`-fsyntax-only` passed, `-emit-llvm` died, and
# the same clang under `ulimit -s 65520` compiled it in 2 s). Past 32 levels
# the emitter now writes a function nothing calls that steps over each struct
# in the order the typedefs were written (`emit/typeorder.hero`), so each is
# converted with its fields already done; and a clang that dies anyway is said
# as one, exit 2, in this compiler's words, with the program's deepest chain
# and without the crash report (`cli/clang_died.hero`, `cli/deep_types.hero`).
# Measured 2026-10-03: the 3,000 variants build at `-O0` in 7.4 s of user time
# and print `0` and `true`; at 5,000 clang's debug information still dies, and
# the build says so. This case is 100 deep, every other level through an
# option, since at `-O2` the build takes 62 s of user time on 1,000 and 175 s
# on 3,000, most of it clang's GVN and inliner, past the harness's 120 s: it
# pins that the function is written, compiles clean and leaves the program
# what it was.

variant R0
    a
        v: i64
    b

variant R1
    a
        inner: R0?
    b

variant R2
    a
        inner: R1
    b

variant R3
    a
        inner: R2?
    b

variant R4
    a
        inner: R3
    b

